.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the command-line client for
.Sy morbstackd ,
the Morbstack daemon
.Pq no separate man page ships for it yet
that runs a single Linux virtual machine on macOS via
.Em Virtualization.framework
and forwards the Docker Engine API out of it.
Most subcommands talk to
.Nm morbstackd
over a local Unix-domain socket; many
.Po
.Cm shares ,
.Cm rosetta status ,
.Cm doctor ,
.Cm diagnose ,
.Cm disk status ,
.Cm ports ,
.Cm context ,
.Cm service ,
.Cm install-cli ,
.Cm uninstall-cli ,
.Cm install-cli-plugins
.Pc
answer from host-side state alone and never require the daemon to be
running.
.Pp
Commands that need the VM running
.Po
.Cm start ,
.Cm stop ,
.Cm suspend ,
.Cm resume ,
.Cm disk grow ,
.Cm k8s enable ,
.Cm k8s disable ,
.Cm k8s kubeconfig
.Pc
will start
.Nm morbstackd
on demand if it is not already running and a sibling
.Nm morbstackd
binary can be found and is correctly signed for virtualization.
Purely observational commands
.Po
.Cm status ,
.Cm shares ,
.Cm rosetta status ,
.Cm doctor ,
.Cm context status
.Pc
never do this: if the daemon is not running they report that fact instead
of starting one just to ask it a question.
.Pp
.Cm mcp ,
.Cm migrate ,
.Cm bench ,
.Cm scan ,
.Cm debug
and
.Cm export
are each implemented in their own Swift module
.Pq Sy MorbMCP , MorbMigrate , MorbBench , MorbScan , MorbExport
that
.Nm
dispatches to with the remaining command-line arguments and the global
.Fl -json
flag, and nothing else.
Their argument grammar and exit codes are defined in those modules, not
in
.Nm Ns 's
own parser; their subcommands and flags are documented below all the
same, read out of those modules rather than out of
.Nm morb --help ,
which never reaches them.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm status
Show daemon and VM state: lifecycle state, guest control channel, Docker
readiness, where container data is stored, active connections, published
ports, and daemon version.
.It Cm start
Boot the VM.
.It Cm stop
Shut the VM down.
Accepts
.Fl -force
to stop without first asking the guest to shut down cleanly.
.It Cm suspend
Release the VM's memory.
On a host that cannot restore saved state this stops cleanly instead, and
the containers do not survive it; the daemon reports that via a note in
the response.
.It Cm resume
Start a VM previously put down with
.Cm suspend ,
cold-booting it when the saved state cannot be restored.
.It Cm shares
List the shared host paths configured in
.Pa config.toml
and, if the daemon is running, whether the guest actually has each one
mounted.
Answerable without the daemon.
.It Cm rosetta Op Cm status
Show whether Rosetta is installed on the host, enabled in the Morbstack
config, and active in the guest.
This is the default when
.Cm rosetta
is given no subcommand.
Answerable without the daemon.
.It Cm rosetta Cm install
Install Rosetta for Linux and enable it in the Morbstack config.
Always prompts for interactive confirmation on a terminal before doing
anything; refuses to run with stdin not a terminal.
Installing Rosetta itself triggers a separate, unavoidable macOS system
licence prompt that
.Nm
does not and cannot answer on the user's behalf.
Accepts
.Fl -print-plan
to print exactly what it would do and exit without doing it.
Does
.Em not
accept
.Fl -force :
this is deliberate, and passing it is a hard error.
See
.Sx OPTIONS .
.It Cm k8s Op Cm status
Show whether the local Kubernetes cluster is installed in the guest,
enabled, and how many nodes/pods are Ready.
This is the default when
.Cm k8s
is given no subcommand.
.It Cm k8s Cm enable
Install the Kubernetes payload into the guest if it is not already
there, then start the cluster.
May start the daemon and the VM.
.It Cm k8s Cm disable
Stop the cluster.
The installed payload and its on-disk state are left in place.
.It Cm k8s Cm diagnose
Report real cluster recovery guidance without changing anything.
.It Cm k8s Cm describe
Read one selected resource through Morbstack's local Kubernetes API:
.Cm describe pod Ar namespace Ar name
or
.Cm describe node Ar name .
Nothing else is enumerated or listed.
.It Cm k8s Cm port-forward
Manage the one selected-Pod loopback TCP lease.
.Cm start Ar namespace Ar pod Ar uid Ar pod-port
opens it and accepts
.Fl -container Ar name
and
.Fl -local-port Ar port ;
.Cm status
shows the current lease;
.Cm cancel Ar lease
cancels only that exact lease.
.It Cm k8s Cm kubeconfig
Write a kubeconfig for the Morbstack cluster to
.Pa ~/.morbstack/kubeconfig .
With
.Fl -merge ,
instead merge a
.Dq morbstack
cluster/user/context into
.Pa ~/.kube/config ,
after asking for confirmation and writing a timestamped backup of that
file first; add
.Fl -switch-context
to also point
.Cm current-context
at
.Dq morbstack
as part of the merge.
.Fl -force
skips the merge confirmation prompt.
.It Cm context Op Cm status
Show whether a
.Dq morbstack
docker context is registered, whether it points at the right socket, and
what the current default context is.
This is the default when
.Cm context
is given no subcommand.
Answerable without the daemon; reads/writes only under the docker CLI's
own config directory
.Pq Ev DOCKER_CONFIG , or Pa ~/.docker No by default .
.It Cm context Cm create
Register a
.Dq morbstack
docker context pointing at the Morbstack Docker socket.
Does not change the current/default context.
Prompts for confirmation unless
.Fl -force
is given.
.It Cm context Cm use
Make
.Dq morbstack
the current/default docker context.
Always prompts for interactive confirmation — this command has no
non-interactive form, regardless of
.Fl -force ;
that flag only lifts the refusal to replace another
.Em explicit
non-default context.
Refuses to run if the context is not already registered
.Pq run Cm context create No first .
.It Cm service Op Cm status
Show whether Morbstack's per-user background LaunchAgent is registered,
whether it still needs approval in Login Items, and whether the control
socket is being answered.
This is the default when
.Cm service
is given no subcommand.
.Cm service enable
registers the signed app's LaunchAgent;
.Cm service disable
unregisters it without stopping a manually started daemon;
.Cm service settings
opens System Settings > Login Items.
.Cm service
takes exactly one action word and no flags of its own.
.It Cm diagnose
Collect a redacted, reviewable support bundle from host metadata,
sanitized
.Cm doctor
checks, and bounded tails of Morbstack-owned text logs.
Never starts the daemon and never contacts the VM.
.Fl -output Ar directory
writes it below an absolute or
.Pa ~/
directory instead of the default location.
Review
.Pa README.txt
and
.Pa report.json
inside the bundle before sharing it.
.It Cm disk Op Cm status
Show the VM disk image path, its configured and current capacity, and
whether a safe growth is possible.
This is the default when
.Cm disk
is given no subcommand, and it is answerable without the daemon.
.It Cm disk Cm grow Ar GiB
Grow an existing disk to an explicit positive target in GiB and verify
the guest filesystem afterwards.
Morbstack never shrinks a disk; a smaller target is a hard error, as is
a target that does not match a pending growth recovery.
.It Cm ports Op Cm check
Check whether one or more loopback endpoints are currently free, before
a
.Cm docker run -p .
Takes
.Fl -tcp Ar port
and
.Fl -udp Ar port ,
repeatably, and requires at least one.
.Cm check
is the only subcommand and is also the default.
The result is a point-in-time snapshot of 127.0.0.1, never a
reservation, and it neither starts nor contacts the daemon.
Exits 2 if any checked endpoint is unavailable.
.It Cm install-cli
The complete per-user CLI setup: symlink the bundled
.Pa docker ,
.Pa docker-compose
and
.Pa docker-buildx
into
.Pa ~/.morbstack/bin
and
.Pa ~/.docker/cli-plugins ,
register the
.Dq morbstack
docker context, and create the per-user discovery socket.
Host-only: it never starts a VM or touches Docker data.
Accepts
.Fl -print-plan
to preview,
.Fl -force
to apply the printed plan without the prompt, and
.Fl -make-default
to put
.Pa ~/.morbstack/bin
before an existing
.Pa docker
in the login profile's PATH.
.It Cm uninstall-cli
Remove only what
.Cm install-cli
owns: Morbstack's own symlinks, the exact managed PATH block, the
user-owned discovery socket link, and the
.Dq morbstack
context when it still points at Morbstack's socket.
It does not remove
.Pa Morbstack.app ,
.Pa ~/.morbstack/data ,
images, volumes, or another Docker installation.
Accepts
.Fl -print-plan
and
.Fl -force .
.It Cm install-cli-plugins
Legacy: symlink only
.Pa docker-compose
and
.Pa docker-buildx
into
.Pa ~/.docker/cli-plugins .
.Cm install-cli
is the current command and does this as part of its own plan.
Accepts
.Fl -print-plan
to preview without acting, and
.Fl -force
to skip the confirmation prompt.
Fails if no plugin binaries can be found next to the
.Nm
executable or under a
.Pa dist/host-bin
checkout.
.It Cm mcp
Model Context Protocol server; read-only unless explicitly granted more.
.Cm mcp serve
runs the server over stdin/stdout;
.Cm mcp init
writes
.Pa ~/.morbstack/mcp.toml
as an empty read-only-by-default profile and accepts
.Fl -force
to replace an existing one;
.Cm mcp permissions
prints every tool's effective permission and where that decision came
from.
.Cm serve
and
.Cm permissions
accept
.Fl -allow Ar permission ,
repeatably, granting a tool name, a group, or an argument guard.
.Cm mcp serve
rejects
.Fl -json :
it already speaks JSON-RPC on stdout.
Implemented in the
.Sy MorbMCP
module.
.It Cm migrate
Import images, volumes and configuration from another container runtime with
.Fl -from ,
or migrate them OUT of Morbstack into another runtime or socket with
.Fl -to ,
verifying every copied item with the same config-ID and sha256sum checks
.Cm migrate verify
uses.
.Cm detect
.Pq the default
surveys local runtimes and
.Cm config
inspects the Docker CLI configuration; both are read-only and take no
flags.
.Cm plan
derives a read-only comparison
.Pq Fl -from , Fl -filter , Fl -all ;
.Cm run
imports an explicitly selected image set
.Po
.Fl -from ,
.Fl -image ,
.Fl -all-images ,
.Fl -dry-run ,
.Fl -yes
.Pc ;
.Cm images
and
.Cm volumes
copy in bulk
.Po
.Fl -from ,
.Fl -filter ,
.Fl -all
.Pq images only ,
.Fl -overwrite
.Pq volumes only, and always rejected ,
.Fl -dry-run ,
.Fl -yes
.Pc ;
.Cm verify
compares the two engines
.Po
.Fl -from ,
.Fl -images ,
.Fl -volumes ,
.Fl -report ,
.Fl -yes
.Pc .
.Fl -to Ar runtime | socket
takes only
.Fl -dry-run
and
.Fl -yes ;
combining it with
.Fl -json
requires
.Fl -yes ,
since a confirmation prompt cannot share JSON stdout.
Option values are passed as
.Ar --name value ,
never
.Ar --name=value .
Implemented in the
.Sy MorbMigrate
module.
.It Cm bench
Run the open benchmark suite and report the numbers.
.Cm list
shows published targets and implementation status;
.Cm history
.Op Fl -limit Ar count
shows saved runs;
.Cm compare Ar baseline Ar candidate
compares two saved runs by path, id,
.Cm latest
or
.Cm previous .
.Cm run
is the only subcommand that measures anything and accepts
.Fl -only Ar names ,
.Fl -runs Ar count ,
.Fl -window Ar seconds
and
.Fl -dry-run .
Implemented in the
.Sy MorbBench
module.
.It Cm scan
SBOM and CVE scan a local image, entirely on this machine: the image is
exported through the Engine socket, an SBOM is generated with
.Xr syft 1 ,
and the SBOM is scanned with
.Xr grype 1 .
Image and SBOM data are never uploaded.
Takes one local image reference plus
.Fl -check ,
.Fl -offline ,
.Fl -sbom-only ,
.Fl -sbom Ar path ,
.Fl -fail-on Ar severity
and
.Fl -all .
.Fl -check
reports the local prerequisites only and contacts neither the engine nor
the network.
Implemented in the
.Sy MorbScan
module.
.It Cm export
Write an already-local image or named-volume archive to a user-selected
file, or with
.Fl -all ,
every local tagged image as one archive per image into a directory that a
stock
.Nm docker load
restores.
.Cm export image Ar reference Fl -output Ar path
saves one image through a single
.Pa GET /images/get ;
.Cm export volume Ar name Fl -output Ar path
archives one existing local-driver volume through one owned, stopped,
read-only helper container and never pulls the helper image;
.Fl -all Fl -output Ar directory
writes every local tagged image plus a
.Pa MANIFEST.txt .
.Fl -output
is required and its parent directory must already exist; an existing
file is refused unless
.Fl -replace
is explicit.
Implemented in the
.Sy MorbExport
module.
.It Cm debug
Inspect whether Morbstack can safely offer a toolbox session for a
container.
It does
.Em not
open a shell.
.Cm debug check
.Op Fl -manifest Ar path
reads one local toolbox descriptor and contacts neither Docker nor a
network;
.Cm debug Op Cm plan
.Ar container
issues one read-only container-inspect request and then lists the exact
actions it did not perform.
A toolbox shell for a distroless container is not implemented, and
Morbstack deliberately does not present a plain
.Cm docker exec
as one: no pinned and verified toolbox asset, network-consent policy,
isolated-session policy, or full-duplex terminal bridge exists yet.
Both forms exit 2, because neither can make a toolbox available.
Implemented in the
.Sy MorbScan
module.
.It Cm version
Print the CLI version, and the daemon's version if it can be reached.
Never fails just because nothing is running.
.It Cm doctor
Diagnose the host: signature/entitlement checks, kernel/initrd presence,
Rosetta support, and similar preflight facts.
Works without the daemon.
Exits 2 if any check is unhealthy.
.It Cm reset-disk
Delete the Docker data disk image
.Pq Pa ~/.morbstack/data/disk.img
and nothing else under
.Pa ~/.morbstack ,
so every image, container and volume in the VM is gone on the next
.Cm start .
Refuses to run while the VM is in any state other than
.Dq stopped
or
.Dq error .
Prompts for interactive confirmation unless
.Fl -force
is given.
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -json
Emit raw JSON instead of human-readable output.
Recognized anywhere on the command line, not only after the command; it
is stripped from the argument list before the command itself is even
read, so
.Nm morb --json status
and
.Nm morb status --json
are identical — and this holds even for
.Cm mcp , migrate , bench , scan , export
and
.Cm debug ,
which receive the flag as a separate parameter rather than as an
argument, and whose other arguments are otherwise opaque to this manual.
.Cm mcp serve
is the one command that rejects it outright.
.It Fl -force
Skip a confirmation prompt, with a command-dependent meaning:
.Bl -tag -width "reset-disk, install-cli-plugins"
.It Cm stop
Skip asking the guest to shut down cleanly first.
.It Cm reset-disk , context create , install-cli , uninstall-cli , install-cli-plugins , mcp init
Skip the interactive
.Dq are you sure
prompt.
.It Cm context use
Does
.Em not
skip the confirmation prompt — that command always asks.
It only lifts the refusal to replace another explicit non-default
context.
.It Cm k8s kubeconfig Fl -merge
Skip that merge's confirmation prompt.
.El
.Pp
On every other command
.Po
.Cm start , suspend , resume , k8s status , k8s enable , k8s disable ,
.Cm context status
.Pc
.Fl -force
is silently ignored, not rejected: it is simply never read by the
parser for those commands, and no error is produced.
It is deliberately
.Em refused
.Pq a hard error, exit 2
by
.Cm rosetta install ,
which installs system software under Apple's licence and therefore
always asks the person at the keyboard regardless of any flag; use
.Fl -print-plan
to preview it, or run
.Xr softwareupdate 8
.Fl -install-rosetta
directly for an unattended install.
.It Fl -print-plan
Print the exact steps a command would take and exit without taking them.
Valid for
.Cm rosetta install ,
.Cm install-cli ,
.Cm uninstall-cli
and
.Cm install-cli-plugins
only.
.It Fl -make-default
Valid only for
.Cm install-cli .
Add
.Pa ~/.morbstack/bin
to the login profile's PATH ahead of an existing
.Pa docker ,
instead of leaving that one first.
.It Fl -output Ar directory
Valid only for
.Cm diagnose .
Write the support bundle below this directory, which must be absolute or
begin with
.Pa ~/ .
.It Fl -merge
Valid only for
.Cm k8s kubeconfig .
Merge the Morbstack context into
.Pa ~/.kube/config
instead of only writing the standalone kubeconfig file.
.It Fl -switch-context
Valid only for
.Cm k8s kubeconfig
alongside
.Fl -merge .
Also switch
.Cm current-context
to
.Dq morbstack
as part of the merge.
This flag exists and is honored by
.Nm ,
but is not mentioned anywhere in
.Nm morb --help Ns 's
own usage text.
.It Fl -help , Fl h
Print the top-level usage summary and exit 0.
Recognized anywhere on the command line and checked before any
subcommand is parsed, so it always prints the same global summary rather
than help for the specific subcommand it follows;
.Nm morb k8s kubeconfig --help
and
.Nm morb mcp --help
both print the exact same text as
.Nm morb --help .
.Fl h
works identically to
.Fl -help
but is not listed in
.Nm morb --help Ns 's
own OPTIONS section.
Because of this, the modules that
.Nm
dispatches to are never reached by
.Fl -help ;
use the bare word
.Cm help
instead
.Pq Nm morb mcp help , Nm morb migrate help , Nm morb bench help , Nm morb scan help , Nm morb export help , Nm morb debug help .
.El
.Pp
Every other flag documented above belongs to exactly one command or
subcommand and is listed with it in
.Sx COMMANDS .
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Nm Ns 's
own argument parser and command dispatch
.Pq mac/Sources/morb/main.swift
do not read any environment variables directly; every path it uses
itself comes from a fixed, compiled-in location under
.Pa ~/.morbstack .
.Cm context Ns 's
subcommands, and the context work
.Cm install-cli
and
.Cm uninstall-cli
do, honor the docker CLI's own
.Ev DOCKER_CONFIG
convention for locating the docker config directory
.Pq default Pa ~/.docker ,
per that command's own implementation.
Whether
.Cm mcp , migrate , bench , scan , debug
or
.Cm export
read any environment variables is not knowable from
.Nm Ns 's
own source; each is implemented in a separate module outside the scope
this manual could verify.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "~/.morbstack/run/morbstackd.sock"
.It Pa ~/.morbstack/run/docker.sock
Unix-domain socket that relays the Docker Engine API out of the guest.
Point
.Ev DOCKER_HOST
at it, e.g.
.Dl DOCKER_HOST=unix://$HOME/.morbstack/run/docker.sock docker ps
.It Pa ~/.morbstack/run/morbstackd.sock
Unix-domain control socket
.Nm
uses to talk to
.Nm morbstackd
(newline-delimited JSON).
.It Pa ~/.morbstack/bin
Where
.Cm install-cli
symlinks the bundled
.Pa docker .
.It Pa ~/.morbstack/mcp.toml
The Model Context Protocol permission profile, created by
.Cm mcp init
and explained by
.Cm mcp permissions .
.It Pa ~/.morbstack/kubeconfig
Kubeconfig written by
.Cm k8s kubeconfig .
.It Pa ~/.morbstack/data/disk.img
The Docker data disk image; deleted by
.Cm reset-disk ,
inspected and grown by
.Cm disk .
.It Pa ~/.morbstack/config.toml
Host-side configuration, including
.Cm shared_paths
and the
.Cm rosetta
setting toggled by
.Cm rosetta install .
.It Pa ~/.kube/config
The user's own kubectl config, edited only by
.Cm k8s kubeconfig --merge ,
and only after asking and taking a timestamped backup.
.It Pa ~/.docker/cli-plugins
Where
.Cm install-cli
and
.Cm install-cli-plugins
symlink
.Pa docker-compose
and
.Pa docker-buildx .
.It Pa ~/.docker
The docker CLI's own config directory
.Pq or Ev DOCKER_CONFIG , if set ,
where
.Cm context
registers and switches the
.Dq morbstack
context.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It 0
Success.
.It 1
.Nm morbstackd
could not be reached: it was not running, no sibling
.Nm morbstackd
binary was found or it was not signed for virtualization, or it could
not be started or bound its socket in time.
.It 2
The command ran but failed: an unknown command or subcommand, a rejected
flag combination
.Pq e.g. Cm rosetta install Fl -force ,
a cancelled confirmation prompt, a check that
.Cm doctor
reports unhealthy, an unavailable endpoint reported by
.Cm ports ,
or a daemon-reported failure.
.El
.Pp
This is the convention
.Nm Ns 's
own code documents and follows for every command it parses directly.
.Cm mcp , migrate , bench , scan , debug
and
.Cm export
each return whatever exit code their own module computes, which
.Nm
merely forwards unchanged; that code was not verified here to follow the
same 0/1/2 convention.
.Cm debug
in particular returns 2 for every successful invocation as well: it
reports that no toolbox is available, which is never a success.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Boot the VM and check on it
.Dl morb start
.Dl morb status
.It Set the docker CLI up once, for this user only
.Dl morb install-cli --print-plan
.Dl morb install-cli
.It Run a container through the relayed Docker socket
.Dl DOCKER_HOST=unix://$HOME/.morbstack/run/docker.sock docker run --rm hello-world
.It Check a host port is free before publishing it
.Dl morb ports check --tcp 8080 --udp 5353
.It Inspect and grow the VM disk
.Dl morb disk status
.Dl morb disk grow 120
.It Collect a redacted support bundle
.Dl morb diagnose --output ~/Desktop
.It Preview a Rosetta install without doing it
.Dl morb rosetta install --print-plan
.It Bring up the local Kubernetes cluster and use it
.Dl morb k8s enable
.Dl morb k8s kubeconfig --merge --switch-context
.Dl kubectl get nodes
.It Scan a local image without uploading anything
.Dl morb scan --check
.Dl morb scan --fail-on high myimage:latest
.It Archive an image to a file
.Dl morb export image myimage:latest --output ~/Desktop/myimage.tar
.It Get machine-readable status for scripting
.Dl morb status --json
.It Start over with an empty Docker data disk
.Dl morb stop
.Dl morb reset-disk --force
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr docker 1 ,
.Xr docker-buildx 1 ,
.Xr docker-compose 1 ,
.Xr grype 1 ,
.Xr kubectl 1 ,
.Xr syft 1 ,
.Xr softwareupdate 8
